{"id":"cdph-actions-after-june-2024","title":"State citations and penalties to November 2026: the case homes and San Francisco homes","question":"What did the State health department issue to the nursing-home case's homes, and to San Francisco homes, after the archived enforcement file ends in June 2024?","finding":"From January 2021 to 13 November 2026 the State issued 114 citations and penalties to 32 of the 42 case homes (66 after the archived file ends on 2024-06-28); 54 were nursing-hours penalties; final amounts $2.0 million. The 19 low-staff case homes with actions received 75 (46 after June 2024), 35 of them nursing-hours penalties (22 after June 2024). San Francisco homes: 42 actions at 12 homes, 2 class AA and 1 class A citations, $1.1 million.","how":"Rows of the State Enforcement Actions dashboard details export (all counties, penalty issue dates 5 January 2021 to 13 November 2026), matched to homes by the State facility number (FACID) from the licence listing. \"Nursing-hours penalty\" is penalty type \"AP - 3.2 NHPPD\" (the 3.5 / 3.2 direct-care hours rule). Check: 3847 of the 3916 dashboard rows issued by 2024-06-28 are also in the archived file; all 318 rows of the five-county export are in the all-county export.","limits":"A citation is a finding by the State but may be appealed, reduced or dismissed (\"Open\" rows are not final); amounts here are the dashboard's final amounts due, which can still change. Larger homes are inspected and cited more often. Penalties for nursing hours are assessed on audited staffing periods that can be two or more years before the issue date. Complaint narratives and complaint counts are not in these files.","tier":"OFFICIAL","columns":[{"k":"home","t":"Home (name in the State file)","type":"org"},{"k":"county","t":"County","type":"text"},{"k":"group","t":"Group","type":"text"},{"k":"actions","t":"Actions 2021-2026","type":"int"},{"k":"afterJune2024","t":"After June 2024","type":"int"},{"k":"classAA","t":"Class AA","ty